  <section class="bench" aria-labelledby="v-lc">
    <div class="bench-head"><h2 id="v-lc">12 · Le Châtelier as a concentration–time graph</h2><span class="hint">PCl₅(g) ⇌ PCl₃(g) + Cl₂(g), K<sub>c</sub> = 0.042</span></div>
    <p style="max-width:68ch">The classic textbook picture: flat lines (equilibrium), a sudden jump when you apply a stress, then curves that bend back and settle at a <b>new</b> equilibrium. The system only partly undoes the stress.</p>
