["Isobaric","Constant P: q(p) = ΔH = nC(p)ΔT."],
["Cp vs Cv","Cp = Cv + R for an ideal gas."],
["Enthalpy","ΔH = ΔE + Δ(PV) = q at constant pressure."],
["ΔH from ΔE","ΔH = ΔE + Δn(g)RT; Δn(g) = gas moles of products − reactants."],
["Bomb calorimeter","Constant volume → measures ΔE (q(v))."],
["Coffee-cup calorimeter","Constant pressure → measures ΔH (q(p))."],
["Calorimetry equations","q = CΔT; q = mcΔT; q(rxn) = −q(calorimeter)."],
["ΔH°f","Enthalpy to form 1 mol of compound from elements in standard states. Elements = 0."],
["ΔH from ΔH°f","ΔH = ΣnΔH°f(products) − ΣmΔH°f(reactants)."],
["Hess's law","ΔH of a sum = sum of the ΔHs. Reverse → flip sign; multiply → multiply ΔH."],
["Bond enthalpy","Energy to break 1 mol of a bond (gas). ΔH ≈ Σ broken − Σ formed. Approximate."],
